      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T01:27:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There shouldn\u0027t be an alias from \"sdk\" to \"\", the \"sdk\" variant is compiled for portability, and anything requesting the portable variant shouldn\u0027t be given a non-portable variant.  If a module does not have a portable variant isn\u0027t it not suitable for distributing in the SDK, and the right fix is to add sdk_version to the modules with errors?",
